{{- /*
  ~/.config/caelestia/cli.json — chezmoi-managed.
  Configures caelestia-cli's own behaviour: screenshot/record args, theming
  toggles, "toggle" workspace app definitions, and even the dots repo
  URL/branch it tracks. Full example config:
  https://github.com/caelestia-dots/cli#configuring
  Starts empty on purpose -- fill in real overrides once caelestia is
  installed and you know what you want to change.

  theme.enableChromium is off: `caelestia scheme set` then runs
  `brave --refresh-platform-policy --no-startup-window`, which never exits
  with Brave 154 (reproduced on deep-thought and hitchhiker), hanging the
  command. Brave still reads the already-written policy file in
  /etc/brave/policies/managed on startup. Re-enable once fixed upstream.
*/ -}}
{
  "theme": {
    "enableChromium": false
  }
}
